failure_location.quote:
Similar to the unconditional DDPM, we perform the training by maximizing the VLB of the conditional log likelihood
\begin{equation*}
-\log q_{\theta}(u_0 | a) \leq -\text{VLB}(\theta; a) \triangleq \mathbb{E}_{p(u_{0:T}|a)}\left[\log \frac{p(u_{1:T} | u_0)}{q_{\theta}(u_{0:T}|a)}    \right].
\end{equation*}

\begin{equation}\label{eqn:cov}
\Sigma_{\theta}(t, u_t, a) 
= \begin{cases}
\dfrac{1 - \bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1 - \bar{\alpha}_t}\beta_t \mathbf{I} & 
       \mbox{Noise free observation,}\\[8pt]
\beta_t \mathbf{I} & \mbox{Observations with additive Gaussian noise.}
         \end{cases}
\end{equation}

We evaluate 
the prediction accuracy and uncertainty of the model $\SOPA$ 
by the mean relative $L_2$-error (MRLE) and the mean standard deviation (MSTD) that are defined by
\begin{equation*}
\frac{1}{|\mathcal{\widetilde{D}}|} \sum_{(a, u) \in \mathcal{\widetilde{D}}} \frac{\|\mbox{mean}(\{\SOPA^{(n)}(a)\}_{n=1}^{N_s}) - u \|_2}{\|u\|_2}\, \quad\mbox{and}\quad 
\frac{1}{|\mathcal{\widetilde{D}}|} \sum_{(a, u) \in \mathcal{\widetilde{D}}}
\frac{\|\mbox{std}(\{\SOPA^{(n)}(a) \}_{n=1}^{N_s}) \|_2}{N_s}\,,
\end{equation*}
respectively.
